# Copy to .dev.vars (gitignored). NEVER commit real values. Production: `npx wrangler secret put NAME`.
# Mock mode: serves fixtures, fakes auth as the fixture user, mocks AI/GitHub. No accounts needed.
HAKIT_MOCKS=1
APP_URL=http://localhost:5173

# Sessions & token encryption (generate: openssl rand -base64 32)
SESSION_SECRET=
TOKEN_ENC_KEY=

# GitHub App "Hakit Dev" (docs/SETUP.md §4). Private key must be PKCS#8, newlines as \n.
GITHUB_APP_ID=
GITHUB_APP_SLUG=
GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=
GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET=
GITHUB_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
GITHUB_APP_PRIVATE_KEY=

# AI runs on Workers AI through the AI binding in wrangler.jsonc; no key needed. Real mode locally
# calls your Cloudflare account (`wrangler login`). Optional fallbacks, used only when set:
# GEMINI_API_KEY=
# HF_TOKEN=

# Live checks and evals outside the worker (check:llm, eval:planning, check:embeddings) call Workers AI
# over REST with these. Token needs Workers AI read + edit.
# CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=
# CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=

# E2E only (T-701): enables POST /api/v1/auth/test-login. Never set in production.
# E2E_LOGIN_SECRET=

# DB scripts read DATABASE_URL from packages/db/.env (see packages/db/.env.example).
# Real mode locally: export CLOUDFLARE_HYPERDRIVE_LOCAL_CONNECTION_STRING_HYPERDRIVE (docs/SETUP.md §3).
